++++

+  download your current nginx version source code 
+  run nginx -V to copy configure parameters. 
+  copy the parameters and run configure with the path to the  module    source  for example : 

++++

  `./configure  --add-dynamic-module=/opt/nginx/provallo-nginx-module  --add-module=/opt/nginx/provallo-nginx-module --with-cc-opt='-g -O2 -ffile-prefix-map=/build/nginx-zctdR4/nginx-1.18.0=. -flto=auto -ffat-lto-objects -flto=auto -ffat-lto-objects -fstack-protector-strong -Wformat -Werror=format-security -fPIC -Wdate-time -D_FORTIFY_SOURCE=2' --with-ld-opt='-Wl,-Bsymbolic-functions -flto=auto -ffat-lto-objects -flto=auto -Wl,-z,relro -Wl,-z,now -fPIC' --prefix=/usr/share/nginx --conf-path=/etc/nginx/nginx.conf --http-log-path=/var/log/nginx/access.log --error-log-path=/var/log/nginx/error.log --lock-path=/var/lock/nginx.lock --pid-path=/run/nginx.pid --modules-path=/usr/lib/nginx/modules --http-client-body-temp-path=/var/lib/nginx/body --http-fastcgi-temp-path=/var/lib/nginx/fastcgi --http-proxy-temp-path=/var/lib/nginx/proxy --http-scgi-temp-path=/var/lib/nginx/scgi --http-uwsgi-temp-path=/var/lib/nginx/uwsgi --with-compat --with-debug --with-pcre-jit --with-http_ssl_module --with-http_stub_status_module --with-http_realip_module --with-http_auth_request_module --with-http_v2_module --with-http_dav_module --with-http_slice_module --with-threads --add-dynamic-module=/build/nginx-zctdR4/nginx-1.18.0/debian/modules/http-geoip2 --with-http_addition_module --with-http_gunzip_module --with-http_gzip_static_module --with-http_sub_module`

   you can use a symbolic link (``ln -s``) to match the path to the downloaded source location. 



   if everything is successful, you will be able to see : 
 
   ``
      checking for getaddrinfo() ... found 
      configuring additional modules [b]
      adding module in /opt/nginx/provallo-nginx-module 
      checking for getaddrinfo() ... found 
      \+ provallo_nginx was configured 
      configuring additional dynamic modules 
      adding module in /opt/nginx/provallo-nginx-module 
      checking for getaddrinfo() ... found 
    `` 
+ run make on the nginx build folder : 

   `make -j8 modules` 
   if successfull you should see something like : 
   ` make[1]: Leaving directory '/opt/nginx/nginx-1.23.future ` 
   
   you can either `make install` or copy the module to the modules folder 
   `sudo cp objs/provallo_nginx.so /usr/share/nginx/modules/provallo_nginx.so`


+  add location entry on your nginx file for the extensions' output: 
   
   ```
   server {
        listen 127.0.0.1:8080;
        listen [::1]:8080;
        server_name localhost;
        location /{

                provallo_nginx;
                provallo_nginx_status 201;
                provallo_nginx_text "$arg_foo bar\n";
        }
      }


   ```
+ validate the configuration with  `nginx -t` , if everything works fine reload the service configuration with  : `nginx -s reload`  


+ validate the service response with curl/wget over the server's location path make sure response is valid (expect 200 server response with : `provallo engine is up` or something similar before enough data is accumulated)

+ check nginx statistics modules for provallo's extension metrics (icmp,udp,etc...)
 **extension structure** 

